{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>King.</b> It is Moses, whom the heads of the people heard the Torah stated from his mouth. The meaning is that he was like a king, and the heads of the tribes gathered to him. This interpretation is supported by what Scripture says, that the Torah was given to the priests — who are, in my opinion, 'all his holy ones' — 'in your hand,' and 'to all the elders of Israel' — this is 'the heads of the people assembled.' There too it is written, 'Assemble to me all the heads of your tribes.' And Rabbi Judah Halevi, of blessed memory, said that 'king' alludes to the Torah, and so he would interpret 'there was no king in Israel.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:20.325858698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}